  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements :</p><p>Statement-I : If BOD is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ppm</mi></math> and dissolved oxygen is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ppm</mi></math> , then it is a good quality water.</p><p>Statement-II : If the concentration of zinc and nitrate salts are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ppm</mi></math> each, then it can be a good quality water.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "fBQlE",
      "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sEhcq",
      "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ovVim",
      "text": "Both the statements I and II are incorrect",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tlloH",
      "text": "Both the statements I and II are correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Drinking water has a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BOD</mi></math> level of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ppm</mi></math>. When the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BOD</mi></math> value of water is in the range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ppm</mi></math>, the water is moderately clean. Polluted water has a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BOD</mi></math> value in the range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ppm</mi></math>.&nbsp;Healthy water should generally have dissolved oxygen concentrations above&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mg</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p><p>Drinking water with concentrations of nitrate (measured as nitrate-nitrogen) below <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mg</mi></math>&nbsp;of nitrate per liter of water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mg</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>) is considered safe.&nbsp;Permissible limit of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi></math>&nbsp;in potable water is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ppm</mi></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
